# What this repository is for, and therefore what it does NOT hold.
#
# The tracked content is SOURCE: C, headers, Makefiles, shell and Tcl, and the
# documents that explain them.  Two other kinds of file live in this tree and
# neither belongs in history:
#
#   BUILD OUTPUT      reproducible from the source beside it.
#   MEASUREMENT DATA  2.2 GB of ILA captures and waveforms under hwdef/test and
#                     hw/.  These are evidence, and valuable — hwdef/README.md
#                     cites them by name — but a capture is an observation of one
#                     run, not a thing a later commit can change.  Tracking them
#                     would make a clone unusable to protect files nothing edits.
#
# So captures stay on disk, untracked, and the READMEs that cite them stay in git.

# ------------------------------------------------------------- build output ---
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.d

# Test programs.  Each is an extensionless file named after the .c beside it, so
# the rule is "ignore what has no extension here" rather than a list that would
# go stale the first time a test is added.
sw/lib/test/*
!sw/lib/test/*.*
!sw/lib/test/Makefile
sw/runtime/test/*
!sw/runtime/test/*.*
!sw/runtime/test/Makefile
runtime/test/*
!runtime/test/*.*
!runtime/test/Makefile
hwdef/test/*
!hwdef/test/*/
!hwdef/test/*.*
!hwdef/test/Makefile

# Generated by hwdef/gen_config.sh from platform/*.conf — the .conf is the source.
hwdef/pim_config.h

# ---------------------------------------------------- measurement / captures --
*.csv
*.vcd
*.wdb
*.wcfg
*.ila
*.ltx
*.dmp
*.dbg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- bitstreams --
*.pdi
*.bit
*.xsa
*.bin
*.elf

# ...EXCEPT the ones under hw/, which are tracked on purpose.
#
# They are build output like everything else above, and the argument that keeps
# them out does not apply: nobody here can rebuild them.  The Vivado project that
# produced each image is not in this tree, so a PDI is the only form the image
# exists in, and scripts/reprogram.sh names one by path for every channel — a
# clone without them cannot bring the board up at all.
#
# The .ltx goes with its .pdi because reprogram.sh passes both; the probe file is
# useless without the image it was generated from and vice versa.
!hw/**/*.pdi
!hw/**/*.ltx
*.rtti

# --------------------------------------------------------- vivado / toolchain --
vivado*.jou
vivado*.log
vivado*.str
*.backup.jou
*.backup.log
.Xil/
xsim.dir/
*.pb
*.wdf

# ------------------------------------------------------------- kernel module --
*.ko
*.mod
*.mod.c
*.symvers
*.order
.tmp_versions/
*.cmd

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ editors ---
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
compile_commands.json

# --------------------------------------------------------- machine state -----
# Which platform this particular machine has selected, and the stamp that says
# it was built.  Both are set by platform/select.sh and scripts/setup.sh; the
# .conf files beside them are the source.  `active` is additionally a symlink
# owned by root here, which git would fight over on every checkout.
platform/active
platform/.built

# Vivado's working directory when scripts/reprogram.sh runs.
scripts/logs/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
